  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0231 database is used to store information about football (soccer) teams, stadiums, players, managers, matches, and goals. The database has seven tables: cities, stadiums, teams, players, managers, matches, and goals.\nThe cities table contains information about football cities, including the city name and the country where the city is located. The stadiums table contains information about football stadiums, including the stadium ID, name, city, capacity, and foreign key to the cities table. The teams table contains information about football teams, including the team ID, name, country, stadium, and foreign key to the stadiums table.\nThe players table contains information about football players, including the player ID, first name, last name, nationality, date of birth, team, jersey number, position, height, weight, and foot. The managers table contains information about football managers, including the manager ID, first name, last name, nationality, date of birth, and team.\nThe matches table contains information about football matches, including the match ID, season, date and time, home team, away team, stadium, home team score, away team score, penalty shootout score, attendance, and foreign keys to the teams and stadiums tables. The goals table contains information about football goals, including the goal ID, match ID, player ID, duration, assist, and goal description.\nEach table has primary keys and foreign keys to enforce entity and referential integrity. The primary keys are used to uniquely identify each row in the table, while the foreign keys are used to establish relationships between tables. The tables also have data types, such as VARCHAR, INT, and DATE, and constraints, such as NOT NULL and CHECK, to ensure data consistency and integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project aims to develop and manage a comprehensive SQL database for the UEFA Champions League, covering the years 2016 to 2022. The database is designed to store and organize detailed information related to various aspects of the league, such as football matches, teams, players, stadiums, goals, and managers. This structured data is crucial for generating reports, performing analysis, and facilitating operations and decision-making processes.\n\n Objectives\n\n- Develop a robust database schema that captures essential data about the UEFA Champions League.\n- Ensure efficient storage and retrieval of information related to matches, teams, players, stadiums, goals, and managers.\n- Enable users to execute complex queries for data analysis and reporting.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- UEFA organizers and administrators who require access to detailed league data.\n- Data analysts and statisticians aiming to conduct analyses and generate insights.\n- Developers building applications or systems that need to interface with this database.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Cities Management: Store and manage data about city names and corresponding countries.\n\n2. Stadium Information: \n   - Maintain details of stadiums including ID, name, city, and seating capacity.\n   - Establish a relationship with cities to associate each stadium with a city.\n\n3. Team Profiles:\n   - Store details of football teams including ID, name, country, and home stadium.\n   - Implement relationships to connect teams with their respective stadiums.\n\n4. Player Data:\n   - Record player-specific information such as ID, name, nationality, date of birth, jersey number, position, height, weight, and preferred foot.\n   - Create associations between players and their teams.\n\n5. Manager Details:\n   - Capture manager information including ID, name, nationality, and team management.\n   - Link managers to their respective teams.\n\n6. Match Records:\n   - Document details of matches including ID, season, date and time, participating teams, stadium, scores, penalty shoot-out status, and attendance.\n   - Establish relationships with teams and stadiums for each match.\n\n7. Goal Statistics:\n   - Track every goal scored with information like goal ID, match ID, scoring player, duration, assisting player, and a brief description.\n   - Create connections between goals, matches, and players.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ensure the database supports efficient query execution for up to several thousand entities per table.\n- Maintain data integrity through the use of foreign keys and constraints.\n- Enable scalability to accommodate expanding data volumes over the years 2016-2022.\n- Ensure data consistency and accuracy across all interconnected tables.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0231.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0231\nCREATE TABLE `cities` (\n  `city_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `city_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`city_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stadiums` (\n  `stadium_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `stadium_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `capacity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stadium_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stadiums_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`city_id`) REFERENCES `cities` (`city_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teams` (\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `team_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `stadium_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teams_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`stadium_id`) REFERENCES `stadiums` (`stadium_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `players` (\n  `player_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `jersey_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `height` float NOT NULL,\n  `weight` float NOT NULL,\n  `foot` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`player_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `players_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `managers` (\n  `manager_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nationality` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`manager_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `managers_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `matches` (\n  `match_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `season` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `home_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `away_team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stadium_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `home_team_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `away_team_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `penalty_shootout_score` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `attendance` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`match_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `matches_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`home_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `matches_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`away_team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `matches_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`stadium_id`) REFERENCES `stadiums` (`stadium_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `goals` (\n  `goal_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `match_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `player_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `assist` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `goal_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`goal_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `goals_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`match_id`) REFERENCES `matches` (`match_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `goals_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`player_id`) REFERENCES `players` (`player_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
